{"chunk_id": "93cc0af01bbe", "text": "As Khara advances on Rama\u2019s hermitage with a vast host of titans, ominous portents fill the sky\u2014blood\u2011like rain, strange cries of birds, and Rama\u2019s weapons trembling as if eager for battle. Reading these signs as foretelling the demons\u2019 destruction, Rama orders Lakshmana to take Sita to a hidden mountain cave so he may face the enemy alone. Lakshmana reluctantly obeys. Rama then arms himself in blazing armor, standing solitary on the battlefield and sounding his bow so that the quarters echo. Meanwhile gods, rishis, and celestial beings gather in the sky to witness the coming clash, praying for Rama\u2019s victory yet wondering how a single warrior could defeat fourteen thousand demons. In their eyes he begins to resemble the terrible, avenging god Rudra.\nKhara\u2019s demon army advances on Rama; ominous signs appear, Rama sends Lakshmana and Sita away, and prepares to face fourteen thousand demons alone.\nThemes: impending battle, omens and prophecy, heroic resolve, divine spectatorship, duty and protection", "vector": [0.016790801659226418, -0.031165465712547302, -0.004991768393665552, 0.00621001748368144, 0.0027622701600193977, 0.015392699278891087, -0.03561767563223839, -0.022994032129645348, -0.028667883947491646, -0.026523223146796227, 0.016899392008781433, 0.012535412795841694, -0.005443097557872534, 0.008904418908059597, 0.0009891913505271077, 0.011300195939838886, 0.041264377534389496, -0.02169094607234001, 0.025450890883803368, -0.01374348159879446, -0.0027402127161622047, -0.01446968037635088, 0.00892477948218584, 0.007893170230090618, -0.031817007809877396, -0.010132848285138607, 0.02474505454301834, -0.03445032611489296, 0.006590084172785282, -0.008151072077453136, -0.00656632985919714, -0.026631813496351242, -0.004781374242156744, -0.0066138384863734245, -0.022681834176182747, 0.004323258064687252, 0.006817445624619722, -0.01634286530315876, 0.011347704567015171, -0.010553636588156223, -0.